# a channel's type argument is written in expression position, so anything
# parses there. the constructor used to test only the outer node's kind, and
# a shape it did not recognise came back as the error type without a word —
# the wildcard that satisfies every later comparison, so the program checked
# clean and its recv lowered to a call nothing defines. a shape that is not a
# type at all is now refused where it is written.

fn main():
    ch := Channel[1](2)
    ch.send(1)
    print("{ch.len()}")
